msgid ""
"The coordinate precision of the input is preserved. This requires special "
"handling for datasets with implicit geometry "
"(:class:`~pyvista.RectilinearGrid`, :class:`~pyvista.ImageData`). The "
"underlying ``vtkAppendFilter`` detects point precision by inspecting the "
"input's stored points, but these datasets store their geometry implicitly "
"(per-axis coordinates, or origin and spacing) and have no such points. The "
"filter would otherwise default to single precision and silently downcast "
"double coordinates. A ``RectilinearGrid`` is cast to double precision when "
"any of its coordinate arrays is double; an ``ImageData`` is always cast to "
"double since its origin and spacing are always stored in double precision. "
"See the upstream VTK bug: "
"https://gitlab.kitware.com/vtk/vtk/-/work_items/19965"
msgstr ""

