#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:39
msgid ""
"``'resample-off-axis'``: :meth:`resample` off-axis dimensions of "
"concatenated images to match the input. The on-axis dimension is `not` "
"resampled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:41
msgid ""
"``'resample-match'``: :meth:`resample` all dimensions of concatenated images"
" to match the input dimensions exactly. This is similar to ``'resample-off-"
"axis'``, except the on-axis dimension is `also` resampled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:44
msgid ""
"``'resample-proportional'``: :meth:`resample` concatenated images "
"proportionally to preserve their aspect ratio(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:46
msgid ""
"``'crop-off-axis'``: :meth:`crop` off-axis dimensions of concatenated images"
" to match the input. The on-axis dimension is `not` cropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:48
msgid ""
"``'crop-match'``: Use :meth:`crop` to center-crop concatenated images such "
"that their dimensions match the input dimensions exactly. This is similar to"
" ``'crop-off-axis'``, except the on-axis dimension is `also` cropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.concatenate:51
msgid ""
"``'preserve-extents'``: the extents of all images are preserved and used to "
"place the images in the output. The whole extent of the output is the union "
"of the input whole extents. The origin and spacing is taken from the first "
"input. ``axis`` is not used by this mode."
msgstr ""

