#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels-1
msgid ""
"'external' | 'internal' | 'all' | 'strict_external', default: 'external'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:40
msgid ""
"Style of boundary polygons to generate. ``'internal'`` polygons are "
"generated between two connected foreground regions. ``'external'`` polygons "
"are generated between foreground and background regions. ``'all'``  includes"
" both internal and external boundary polygons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:45
msgid ""
"These styles are generated such that ``internal + external = all``. "
"Internally, the filter computes all boundary polygons by default and then "
"removes any undesired polygons in post-processing. This improves the quality"
" of the output, but can negatively affect the filter's performance since all"
" boundaries are always initially computed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:51
msgid ""
"The ``'strict_external'`` style can be used as a fast alternative to "
"``'external'``. This style `strictly` generates external polygons and does "
"not compute or consider internal boundaries. This computation is fast, but "
"also results in jagged, non-smooth boundaries between regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/core/filters/image_data.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.core.filters.image_data.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels:57
