#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:16
msgid "Crop the image to simplify the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:22
msgid ""
"Plot the cropped image for context. Use "
":meth:`~pyvista.DataSetFilters.color_labels` to generate consistent coloring"
" of the regions for all plots. Negative indexing is used for plotting "
"internal boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:62
msgid ""
"Generate surface contours of the foreground regions and plot it. Note that "
"the ``background_value`` is ``0`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:94
msgid ""
"By default, only external boundary polygons are generated and the returned "
"``'boundary_labels'`` array is a single-component array. The output values "
"match the input label values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:103
msgid ""
"Set ``simplify_output`` to ``False`` to generate a two-component array "
"instead showing the two boundary regions associated with each polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:110
msgid ""
"Show the unique values. Since only ``'external'`` boundaries are generated "
"by default, the second component is always ``0`` (i.e. the "
"``background_value``). Note that all four foreground regions share a "
"boundary with the background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:120
msgid ""
"Repeat the example but this time generate internal contours only. The "
"generated array is 2D by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:127
msgid ""
"Show the unique two-component boundary labels again. From these values we "
"can determine that all foreground regions share an internal boundary with "
"each other `except`  for regions ``1`` and ``3`` since the boundary value "
"``[1, 3]`` is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:139
msgid ""
"Simplify the output so that each internal multi-component boundary value is "
"assigned a unique negative integer value instead. This makes it easier to "
"visualize the result with :meth:`~pyvista.DataSetFilters.color_labels` using"
" the ``negative_indexing`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:178
msgid ""
"Generate contours for all boundaries, and use ``select_outputs`` to filter "
"the output to only include polygons which share a boundary with region "
"``3``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:212
msgid ""
"Note how using ``select_outputs`` preserves the sharp features and boundary "
"labels for non-selected regions. If desired, use ``select_inputs`` instead "
"to completely \"ignore\" non-selected regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:245
msgid ""
"The sharp features are now smoothed and the internal boundaries are now "
"labeled as external boundaries. Note that using ``'all'`` here is optional "
"since using ``select_inputs`` converts previously-internal boundaries into "
"external ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:250
msgid ""
"Do not pad the image with background values before contouring. Since the "
"input image has foreground regions visible at the edges of the image (e.g. "
"the ``+Z`` bound), setting ``pad_background=False`` in this example causes "
"the top and sides of the mesh to be \"open\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:284
msgid ""
"Disable smoothing to generate staircase-like surface. Without smoothing, the"
" surface has quadrilateral cells by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:316
msgid ""
"Keep smoothing enabled but reduce the smoothing scale. A smoothing scale "
"less than one may help preserve sharp features (e.g. corners)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pyvista/doc/source/api/core/_autosummary/pyvista.ImageDataFilters.contour_labels.rst:348
msgid ""
"Use the ``'strict_external'`` style to compute external contours quickly. "
"Note that this produces jagged and non-smooth boundaries between regions, "
