#: of pyvista.DataSetMapper.resolve:4
msgid ""
"A global flag that controls whether the coincident topology (e.g., a line on"
" top of a polygon) is shifted to avoid z-buffer resolution (and hence "
"rendering problems)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/plotting/mapper.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.DataSetMapper.resolve:8
msgid ""
"If not off, there are two methods to choose from. `polygon_offset` uses "
"graphics systems calls to shift polygons, lines, and points from each other."
" `shift_zbuffer` is a legacy method that is used to remap the z-buffer to "
"distinguish vertices, lines, and polygons, but does not always produce "
"acceptable results. You should only use the polygon_offset method (or none) "
"at this point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.14/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pyvista/plotting/mapper.pydocstring
#: of pyvista.DataSetMapper.resolve:22
msgid ""
"Global flag to avoid z-buffer resolution. Must be either `off`, "
"`polygon_offset` or `shift_zbuffer`."
msgstr ""

