":meth:`compose`) can operate in either :meth:`pre_multiply` or "
":meth:`post_multiply` mode. In pre-multiply mode, any additional "
"transformations will occur *before* any transformations represented by the "
"current :attr:`matrix`. In post-multiply mode (the default), the additional "
"transformation will occur *after* any transformations represented by the "
"current matrix."
